  "question": {
    "text": "The curve given by $x+y=e^{x y}$ has a tangent parallel to the Y-axis at the point",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "rz8BM",
      "text": "$(0,1)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LaHZq",
      "text": "$(1,0)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GFFFR",
      "text": "$(1,1)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "X12J1",
      "text": "None of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\because x+y=e^{x y}$<br />Differentiating w.r.t. $x$, we get<br />$1+\\frac{d y}{d x}=e^{x y}\\left[y+x \\frac{d y}{d x}\\right]$<br />$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{d y}{d x}\\left(1-x e^{x y}\\right)=y e^{x y}-1$<br />$\\Rightarrow \\frac{d y}{d x}=\\frac{y e^{x y}-1}{1-x e^{x y}} \\because \\frac{d y}{d x}=\\infty$,<br />as tangent is parallel to $\\mathrm{Y}$-axis<br />$\\Rightarrow 1-x e^{x y}=0$<br />$\\therefore \\mathrm{xe}^{\\mathrm{xy}}=1$<br />This holds, when $x=1$ and $y=0$",
    "image": null
  },
